1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Welcome everybody, welcome to the source code for Wednesday October 20th 2000 and 4 coming to you from the highway between Belgium and the Netherlands.

2
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,000
It's your source code, I'm Adam Curry, welcome everybody to the show.

3
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:48,000
I've got to be honest, I've started today's source code at least five times and couldn't get it the way I wanted to and quite honestly just didn't have the emotional energy to get into it.

4
00:00:49,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Let me explain what happened yesterday, I missed the source code, I wasn't able to tape, let me tell you what happened and again it's taken me quite a while and a lot of conversations with a lot of people before I decided to record today's source code and tell you what I have to say.

5
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Yesterday I went with my sister Tiffany, who's two years younger than I am, we have another sister Willow, she's four years younger than I am, she lives in Italy, she couldn't come with us but we took our mom to the hospital to get the final results of her test.

6
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Yesterday we found out that she is tested positive for lung cancer.

7
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Now you can understand why I didn't cut a source code yesterday.

8
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:55,000
My mom divorced my dad when I was 22, 23 years ago and he also lives in Holland but ever since I've become the man of the family.

9
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,000
And you're supposed to take care of all kinds of stuff.

10
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:18,000
So yesterday going through all this and hearing what the options were and just lending emotional support kind of fell on my shoulders because you got to be strong and got to help everybody through this.

11
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:38,000
It was hard I couldn't bring myself quite yet to record a show and in fact this morning I started recording and I lost it and for the first time in I think more than 20 years I cried like a baby.

12
00:02:38,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Yeah, it's like one of these things and I know that there are hundreds of thousands and millions of people probably tens of millions of people that go through this every single day and families and it affects so many people and many of you listening me will probably have experiences with this and you know kind of what we're going through.

13
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:13,000
So let me give you a little bit of background on what's happening. First of all this is the thing that sucks the most is she looks great. She feels fine.

14
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:30,000
The reason why she went to get went to the doctor was she had a cough that wouldn't go away and they discovered after it took an x-ray lung photo they discovered that she has a tumor low in her right lung.

15
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Which is about six centimeters big at this point from what they can see it is not spread to other parts of her body.

16
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:53,000
It is the non-small cell form of cancer which is not the most aggressive kind it's guess what we call just a regular old fucked up cancer.

17
00:03:53,000 --> 00:04:13,000
And because it's so low and because we can't see any spreading she has a chance after she has a PET scan which is a radioactive scan where they can get even closer look to see if there's any other cell forming anywhere else in her body which they couldn't see on regular CT scans.

18
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:27,000
She has perhaps she has a chance that she can be operated which means they'll either remove half of her right lung or all of her right lung if she has enough lung capacity in the left lung to live a normal life.

19
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:32,000
I have to know that my mom has been a smoker all over life of course.

20
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:46,000
And wouldn't you know that she quit about three quarters of a year ago she has finally quit smoking so of course this is exactly how these things go right like Murphy pops up and says oh yeah.

21
00:04:47,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Should that not be possible then we resort to radiation and chemotherapy now this kind of comes at a difficult moment for for my mom certainly but you know I'm in the midst of a move we're moving to the UK and only four weeks.

22
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Patricia as I think I've mentioned before has heart disease so you know where you think you're riding on top of the world you know and and you've got money and you can buy anything you want and you can do anything you want and there's exciting stuff on the horizon and there's cool stuff happening and podcasting is exploding and.

23
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:38,000
And then life throws you curveball and says hey dude this is not what it's all about this is was really important.

24
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:54,000
So anyway I'm on my way to Amsterdam staying overnight there and I was halfway up the highway and I said you know okay I think I'm ready to talk about this and I pulled off to the side and I'm sitting here.

25
00:05:54,000 --> 00:06:04,000
Kind of parking a lot of a grad of a gas station and just wanted to share this with you because if these podcasts are really going to be.

26
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:10,000
All about life and and there are own personal shows and we can do whatever we want.

27
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:23,000
I think that it's only fair that I can share this with you and of course I talked it over with my mom and everybody else and and they're all totally cool with it and maybe it's a good therapy for me to.

28
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:27,000
To get some of this off my chest so I really appreciate you listening to this.

29
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Okay.

30
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:36,000
I was not going to play any any music in today's show that was not licensed.

31
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:48,000
This is something that we've been talking about the all since we've been doing podcast and I'm certainly the four runner of breaking the rules by playing music which I don't have the rights to play and.

32
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:56,000
And it's unnecessary really when you think about it because you know there's so much music out there and I'm going to hit on that a little bit later on in the show.

33
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:06,000
But I'm just going to break the law one more time if you don't mind playing a song for my mom because we will get through this definitely with a little help from our friends.

